<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06WX">Example <span data-tag="06WX">9.6.8.5</span> <span class="named">(Connective and Truncated Morphisms)</span>.</a> Let $n$ be an integer, let $S_{L}$ denote the collection of all $n$-connective morphisms between Kan complexes (Definition <a data-tag="04GZ" href="/tag/04GZ">3.5.1.13</a>), and let $S_{R}$ denote the collection of all $(n-1)$-truncated morphisms between Kan complexes (Definition <a data-tag="055Z" href="/tag/055Z">3.5.9.1</a>). Then the pair $(S_ L, S_ R)$ is a factorization system on the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$. See Example <a data-tag="06W7" href="/tag/06W7">9.6.6.6</a> and Corollary <a data-tag="05CY" href="/tag/05CY">4.8.7.8</a>. </p>
